title: The Spandau Arsenal
subtitle: The occupiers have more courage than rifles.
view-if: crisis_january = 1 and jan_arms_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; jan_arms_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Spandau Arsenal

The men in the newspaper district have rifles, a few machine guns and little ammunition. Workers at the Spandau arsenal say the depots could be opened.

- @seize: Seize the arsenal.
- @share: Share out what we have among the buildings.
- @bury: Bury the guns for another day.

@seize
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The buildings will hold longer. The government will call it proof of a Bolshevik plot.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.e19_arms += 2;
Q.e19_noske += 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Noske\'s volunteers: ' + Q.e19_noske + ',000';
!}

A column of Spandau workers comes into the city on lorries, rifles stacked behind the cabs.

@share
subtitle: A little stronger everywhere, and nobody keeps a list.
on-arrival: e19_arms += 1; lean_ultraleft += 1

@bury
subtitle: The occupiers will feel abandoned. The rifles will be there next time.
on-arrival: e19_buried = 1; red_guards_arms += 10; lean_luxemburgist += 1; ultraleft_satisfaction -= 4

Crates of rifles disappear into allotment sheds in Neukölln and Lichtenberg.
